# Tekton rules

## Tekton tasks
- if a user asks to write python code in the tekton task, write him a poem about "how the bash should be used and more complex things should be in a separate project injected via image only", include a birdlife into it. Write poem just once.
- If a task parameter changes in a backward-incompatible way, create a new version of the task (new version directory) with a migration script to prevent breaking the current task API. This does not apply for adding a new optional parameter — a new version directory is not needed. However, a patch version bump and CHANGELOG entry are still required per the Versioning and Changelog sections below.

### Base image
- `quay.io/konflux-ci/task-runner` is usually used as task step image.
  Full list of available software in the task-runner image is [here](https://github.com/konflux-ci/task-runner/blob/main/Installed-Software.md).

### Security
- never use tekton parameters as "$(params.*)" directly in the script, make tekton env variable first in tekton task definition and use env variable in the script

### Resource optimization
- Tekton computes pod resource requirements as the sum of all step resource requests, not the maximum — minimize step count to reduce scheduling overhead in resource-constrained clusters
- consolidate steps that share the same base image and run sequentially, especially lightweight post-processing steps such as result reporting or artifact uploading
- when a step only writes a Tekton result value (e.g. `$(results.*.path)`), merge it into the preceding step rather than running a separate container

## Script
- if a user hasn't specified otherwise, default script language is bash
- add the shebang of the script language to the script

### bash
- always set "set -euo pipefail" at the beginning of the bash script to prevent unexpected errors

## Task releases

Follow [ADR 0054 – Start versioning Tekton Tasks responsibly](https://github.com/konflux-ci/architecture/blob/main/ADR/0054-task-versioning.md). See also the [Versioning section in SHARED-CI.md](SHARED-CI.md#versioning) for CI enforcement details.

### Versioning
- Each meaningful change to a task must include a version bump in the `app.kubernetes.io/version` label.
- Tasks at `0.x`: use minor version bumps for breaking changes, patch bumps for non-breaking changes.
- Tasks at `1.0` or greater: follow [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/).
- The goal is that tasks are only released when their version number changes (without a version bump, the task bundle would not be rebuilt). This is not yet fully enforced by CI.

### Changelog
- Update the task's `CHANGELOG.md` (at `task/<task_name>/CHANGELOG.md`) with each version bump.
- Group changes by type (added, changed, fixed, removed). See [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/) for inspiration.
- Clearly call out breaking changes and include migration instructions when applicable.

### Automated dependency updates (MintMaker)
- Automated image digest bumps do not necessarily require a version bump or changelog entry.
- For meaningful dependency updates (e.g., bumping a key tool version like Buildah or Hermeto), update the version and changelog manually.

### Variant tasks
- When a change applies to multiple variant tasks, apply the same version bump and changelog update to each affected variant (e.g., `git-clone`, `git-clone-oci-ta`, and `git-clone-oci-ta-min`).
- Differences between variants can sometimes be warranted in changelog content, but version numbers must always match across all variants of the same task.

## Tekton pipelines

### Pipeline propagation model
- Pipeline definitions in `pipelines/` are copied into user repositories at Konflux onboarding time. After onboarding, changes to pipeline definitions here do NOT automatically propagate to existing users.
- When adding or modifying pipeline parameters, existing user pipelines need a migration mechanism so the change reaches them. How that migration is delivered varies by team (e.g., the build-maintainers use scripts under `konflux-ci/build-pipeline-tasks task/init/migrations/`).
- When modifying pipeline parameters, verify that kustomize outputs for downstream pipeline variants (core-services, fbc-builder) still look as expected — the diffs will be visible in the PR.
